.TH GWU 1 "October 2026" "gwu" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gwu \- initialize and administer a WireGuard server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gwu
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gwu
creates and maintains WireGuard server and peer configuration. Installing the
Debian package does not create a service account or initialize a server.
Administrative commands are run through sudo. Initialization is an explicit
administrative operation.
.SH PRIVILEGES
Commands that read or modify /etc/wireguard or manage WireGuard and traffic
control must be run through sudo. Help, version and completion generation do
not require root privileges.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B wireguard init
Prepare system directories, enable IPv4 forwarding and initialize a default
wg0 server. This command must be run as root.
.TP
.BI "wireguard server install --name " interface " --network " prefix " --port " port
Create and start a WireGuard server with explicit parameters.
.TP
.BI "wireguard user add " user
Add a peer and generate its client configuration.
.TP
.BI "wireguard user remove " user
Remove a peer.
.TP
.BI "wireguard user block " user
Disable a peer without deleting its configuration.
.TP
.BI "wireguard user unblock " user
Enable a blocked peer.
.TP
.B wireguard user list
Display configured peers.
.TP
.BI "wireguard template show " "server|client|gateway"
Display the current WireGuard configuration template.
.TP
.BI "wireguard template set " "server|client|gateway" " --file " path
Replace a configuration template with the contents of a file.
Validate template rendering and Bash hook syntax before replacing the file.
Hooks are not executed during validation.
.TP
.BI "wireguard template reset " "server|client|gateway"
Restore the built-in configuration template.
This explicitly replaces local customizations but does not regenerate the
running WireGuard configuration or restart an interface.
.TP
.BI "qos init --interface " interface " --rate " rate
Generate channel.json and qos.service from local .tmpl without applying QoS.
.TP
.B qos render
Rerender the generated unit from the module templates; preserve channel.json.
.TP
.BI "qos apply --config " path
Apply a shared egress HTB/FQ-CoDel channel through Netlink. Update only the
existing owned class when the rate changes. Does not install a service.
.TP
.BI "qos show --interface " interface
Read actual channel state and ownership.
.TP
.BI "qos down --interface " interface
Remove only the verified owned channel. Refuse unknown qdiscs and old layouts.
.TP
.B version
Display gwu and Go versions.
.SH INITIALIZATION
The built-in server template uses native nftables for IPv4 masquerading.
It creates a per-interface table named gwu_nat_ followed by the hexadecimal
encoding of the interface name. It does not configure forwarding policy or
source routing rules. An existing NAT table with that name causes startup
to fail rather than being overwritten. Existing on-disk templates are not
replaced by a package upgrade; updating them requires an explicit operation.
.PP
Install the package and its dependencies with APT, then initialize explicitly:
.PP
.nf
sudo apt install ./gwu_VERSION_ARCH.deb
sudo gwu wireguard init
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard/gwu/wireguard
Module metadata, client configurations, local templates and generated artifacts.
Only the module layout is supported.
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard/gwu/qos/templates
Editable channel.json.tmpl and qos.service.tmpl. Defaults are embedded.
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard/gwu/qos/generated/qos.service
Generated unit for manual review. Never automatically installed or enabled.
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard/gwu/qos/channel.json
Shared channel prototype configuration: interface and rate.
No per-user bandwidth, upload shaping or ACL.
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard/gwu/qos/state
Ownership records and a process lock. These are not proof against manual
changes by root. Incomplete operations require explicit inspection/recovery.
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard
Live wg-quick interface configuration files. Module-owned files live under
/etc/wireguard/gwu/wireguard and /etc/wireguard/gwu/qos.
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard/gwu/wireguard/templates
Editable server, client and gateway WireGuard module templates.
.TP
.I /etc/sysctl.d/90-gwu.conf
IPv4 forwarding setting created by
.BR "gwu wireguard init" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wg (8),
.BR wg-quick (8),
.BR tc (8),
.BR nft (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
